{
  "id": "COMPOUND:24208 - PROTEIN:5783",
  "verbalization": "Pinostrobin is implicated in the pathogenesis of M19-MEL through a multi-tiered mechanism involving Caspase-5, which is a key target of multiple compounds. The evidence suggests that Pinostrobin acts as a modulator of Caspase-5, which in turn influences the activity of other compounds such as 23-Hydroxy-3-Oxoolean-12-En-27-Oic Acid and 5-Oxobrucine, all of which ultimately target M19-MEL. This indicates a potential pathway where Pinostrobin may exert its effects through Caspase-5, leading to downstream effects on M19-MEL. The consistent presence of Caspase-5 as a common target across different compounds supports the hypothesis that Pinostrobin may interact with Caspase-5 to influence M19-MEL. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of Caspase-5 in mediating the effects of Pinostrobin on M19-MEL, suggesting a mechanistic link that is supported by the observed scores and target relationships.",
